cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use OpenFocus in your work, please cite it as below. See also the repository README for algorithm-specific references."
title: OpenFocus
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Xinzhe
    family-names: Xie
    email: xiexinzheyyy@163.com
    affiliation: Zhejiang University
repository-code: "https://github.com/Xinzhe99/OpenFocus"
url: "https://github.com/Xinzhe99/OpenFocus"
abstract: >-
  OpenFocus is an open-source multi-focus image fusion workstation for
  PyQt6-based desktop use and headless command-line pipelines. It combines
  homography and ECC image registration with five fusion algorithms
  (guided filter, DCT, dual-tree complex wavelet transform, GFG-FGF and
  the StackMFF-V4 deep model), supports 8- and 16-bit stacks, HEIC input,
  batch processing and project files, and ships for Windows and macOS
  (Apple Silicon) as well as through PyPI (`pip install openfocus`).
keywords:
  - image fusion
  - focus stacking
  - multifocus
  - microscopy
  - macro photography
  - image registration
  - ECC
  - PyQt6
